ue":"7.4 ± 0.8","numeric":7.4}}],"logp":[{"abbreviation_in_the_article":"Mono-Pt","value":1.77,"value_relation":"=","std":0.11,"type_authors":"logP","method":"shake-flask","aqueous_phase":"10 mM phosphate buffer","pH":7.4,"temperature_C":25,"doi":"10.1021/acs.jmedchem.1c01690","year":2021,"record_id":"MLDB-001796","detection":"UV-Vis","method_description":"The partition coefficient (log P) for Mono-Pt was measured by the shaking flask method in a 1-octanol/buffer system. Briefly, solutions of Mono-Pt (50, 100, and 150 μM) were prepared in the phosphate buffer (10 mM, pH 7.4) presaturated with 1-octanol. Equal volumes of 1-octanol presaturated with phosphate buffer and solutions of Mono-Pt presaturated with 1-octanol were mixed and placed in a mechanical shaker at room temperature for 24 h. The samples were separated into two phases after centrifugation at 2500 rpm for 20 min. The aqueous layer was carefully separated and the concentration of the solute in the aqueous phase was determined by spectrophotometry (λmax = 261 nm). According to the law of mass conservation, the drug concentration of the corresponding 1-octanol phase and the lipo-hydro partition coefficient Po/w were calculated (Po/w = Co/Cw = Ao/Aw, A stands for absorbance). The log P values were calculated from an average of three independent measurements."}]}